C-BuildSystem

C build system written in C.

works on mac, linux, powershell whatever

pleae look into : https://xt9y.de/c.html

Benchmarks are published as a release after CI is done

install --> git clone ... && cd C-BuildSystem && make && sudo make install
init    --> c init
build   --> c build
run     --> c run
test    --> c test

asset repositories --> add c_git + c_dep_assets; no per-file listing needed

  C_Dependency *models = c_git(b, "models",
      "https://github.com/xt9y-org/MODELS.git", "main");
  c_dep_assets(models);
  c_use(app, models);

  // In application source:
  // #include <casset.h>
  // const char *path = c_asset("models", "spacestation.glb");
  // Nested paths use their exact repository-relative spelling.

  c run                           # all repository files are callable
  c run -- spacestation.glb       # checks out only this Git asset
  c update models                 # update the locked revision for new files

For a build configured to expose ONLY specific files:

  c_dep_asset_only(models, "spacestation.glb"); // direct name
  // or c_dep_asset(models, "path/file.glb", "alias.glb");

Explicit c_dep_asset(...) mappings limit exposed asset names. Sparse,
blobless Git checkout is used only for asset-only c_dep_assets() dependencies.
Header/source dependencies with a linked asset keep their normal full checkout.
Each locked revision and selected asset set has its own source-cache key.
